{"term":"throw up","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:54c22d4a3e6b045223","definition":"Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see throw, up.","example":"Away to the window I flew like a flash,\nTore open the shutters and threw up the sash.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["throw up a brick","throw up the sponge"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/throw_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e7d15beea432c5f562","definition":"To vomit.","example":"The baby threw up all over my shirt.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["chuck up","hurl","upchuck","vomit"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive, informal","register":"ambitransitive, informal","wordFamily":["throw up a brick","throw up the sponge"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/throw_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:95cb9cc7f20275a98a","definition":"To produce or reveal something new or unexpected.","example":"This system has thrown up a few problems.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["throw up a brick","throw up the sponge"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/throw_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2dbfb7a22e9ea8cadc","definition":"To cause something such as dust or water to rise into the air.","example":"The car wheels threw up a shower of stones.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["throw up a brick","throw up the sponge"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionar